--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored source (bundled in this repository)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

BRouter — MIT License
  The `brouter/` module is the pure-Java core of BRouter (the offline routing
  engine behind OsmAnd / Locus / c:geo), vendored from release v1.7.10 so
  OpenCfMoto can compute routes fully on-device with no connection and in a
  single APK (no AIDL to a separately installed BRouter app). It merges BRouter's
  five core modules — brouter-core, brouter-mapaccess, brouter-expressions,
  brouter-codec, brouter-util (all `btools.*` packages) — with the Android app,
  standalone server and map-creator tooling omitted. No BRouter source was
  modified. Original work Copyright (c) BRouter contributors; licensed under the
  MIT License (see brouter/LICENSE for the full text).
  Upstream: https://github.com/abrensch/brouter

  The bundled routing profile (`fastbike.brf`) and tag table (`lookups.dat`) in
  app/src/main/assets/brouter/ are also from BRouter v1.7.10, MIT-licensed.
  BRouter `.rd5` routing segments are downloaded on demand from
  https://brouter.de/brouter/segments4/ — derived from OpenStreetMap data,
  © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). Please be polite with request volume.

